        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(mcp): suppress unhandled error on stderr pipe in stdio transport",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where an MCP stdio child could crash OpenClaw when its piped stderr source stream emitted an error.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe OpenClaw-owned stdio transport now attaches the stderr source-stream listener before piping and forwards failures through the existing non-fatal `Transport.onerror` callback. This matches the adjacent stdin/stdout behavior and preserves stderr diagnostics.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMCP child stderr failures no longer escape as unhandled Node `error` events. Operators still receive the transport error and any stderr diagnostics emitted before the failure.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused regression: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/mcp-stdio-transport.test.ts` (8 passed).\n- Real baseline child-process probe: destroying an unhandled piped `ChildProcess.stderr` stream exited Node with code 1 and `baseline-unhandled-stderr-failure`.\n- Real repaired-path probe using `OpenClawStdioClientTransport` and an actual Node child:\n\n```json\n{\"pidWasReal\":true,\"diagnosticObserved\":true,\"errorObserved\":true,\"processSurvived\":true}\n```\n\n- `oxfmt` and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh structured autoreview reported no accepted or actionable findings.\n- Exact prepared head: `19822fc52e28ec411b2f4700909e40e01339bc16`.\n",
        "branch": "fix/mcp-stdio-stderr-pipe-error-handler",
        "head_sha": "19822fc52e28ec411b2f4700909e40e01339bc16",
